    {
      "block_id": "2605.18130_p5_b21",
      "text": "V3: Self-Distillation Consistency Regularization\nIn clinical ultrasound imaging, common artifacts like acous-\ntic shadowing and speckle noise often lead to inaccurate or\nconflicting bounding boxes. To prevent these noisy predictions\nfrom disrupting the training process, we introduce a self-\ndistillation consistency constraint. Intuitively, this mechanism\nuses reliable, high-confidence predictions to guide and correct\nthe highly uncertain ones. Specifically, based on the calibrated\nweight wfinal\n",
      "bbox": [
        48.96,
        231.66,
        300.02,
        337.83
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        195,
        926,
