    {
      "block_id": "2605.18130_p5_b89",
      "text": "Furthermore, Ltext aux provides the optimization objective\nfor our asymmetric text-prompting strategy and V2 semantic\nre-scoring mechanism. This description-guided auxiliary loss\nexplicitly forces the visual encoder to align with the fine-\ngrained BI-RADS semantic descriptors (e.g., shape, margin)\nprovided during training. By establishing this robust joint\nembedding space, this early cross-modal alignment ensures\nthat the BLIP-2 text features used for computing cosine\nsimilarity in V2 contain rich clinical semantics. Consequently,\nthe automated prompt construction is deeply informed by\nthese semantics, enabling the framework to effectively filter\nout spurious visual artifacts such as acoustic shadows without\nrelying on manual annotations at inference time.\n",
